# sdfblend

- Label: SDF Blend
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 2
- Parameters: 6 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/sdfblend.html
- Summary (EN): SDF Blend merges two Mono signed distance field layers into a single field, so that complex shapes can be built from simpler ones. It offers boolean-style combine modes and optional fillets where the shapes meet.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud SDF Blend fusionne deux couches SDF mono en un seul champ, avec des modes booléens et des congés optionnels à la jonction.

- Inputs meaning: ["sdfA: the first Mono SDF layer", "sdfB: the second Mono SDF layer"]

- Key parameters: ["Mode: Union (encloses both shapes), Intersect (overlap only), Subtract (cuts sdfB out of sdfA), Difference (removes the shared region)", "Fillet: None, Smooth, Round (quarter-circle join) or Chamfer (45-degree bevel)", "Smooth / Round / Chamfer amount: shown for the matching Fillet type", "Re-Normalize: recalculates the distance field after the blend"]

- Caveats: ["Some blend operations leave the distance field values incorrect; enable Re-Normalize to correct them, at the cost of an extra recalculation"]

